@title Famicom Mini - Famicom Mukashi Banashi - Shin Onigashima Zenkouhen (Japan)
@file Famicom Mini - Vol. 26 - Famicom Mukashi Banashi - Shin Onigashima Zenkouhen (J) [o1].gba
@game FFMJ
@chip EEPROM 4Kbit
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# The Disk System version, on the whole 4 MB cartridge image (the archive's
# "[o1]"). The untagged 1 MB file is its first megabyte only: the Disk
# System file directory is at 0x08170000, and on the 1 MB file every
# emulator mirrors sine-table data there, so the boot's file lookup walked
# unmapped memory for good and the screen stayed blank in dingbat and the
# second reference (docs/playtest-bugs.md §100).
# Title, START: the storyteller (さいしょから / せーぶした ところから), A:
# from the start, すこしのしんぼうじゃ while the disk loads, 一しょう, A A
# through the opening text to the command menu in いろりのへや (みる とる
# はなす あける いどう もちもの). START: ここまでを、せーぶするかの?, A
# saves and returns to the title. [load]: DOWN to せーぶした ところから, A
# resumes in いろりのへや at the command menu.
# Seen while authoring: the second reference's title birds and storyteller
# text run a frame behind the other two (title); at saved_title dingbat-bios
# is a frame off both references, which agree (not traced). dingbat and the
# second reference write the same 512-byte file (4 Kbit; the second
# reference sizes it right unaided); mgba writes 8 KB, the same 512 bytes
# then zeros, which the second reference reads as a different save (its
# load of mgba's file is MAJOR, as for Makaimura, §94).
[new]
wait 300
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 120
wait 180
checkpoint start_menu window=30
press A
wait 240
wait 300
checkpoint chapter1 window=30
press A
wait 240
press A
wait 240
checkpoint commands window=30
press START
wait 60
wait 120
checkpoint save_prompt window=30
press A
wait 240
wait 300
checkpoint saved_title window=30

[load]
wait 300
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 120
wait 180
press DOWN
wait 20
checkpoint continue_selected window=30
press A
wait 240
wait 300
checkpoint resumed window=30
